.TH LocalTranslate "1" "2026-06-06" "LocalTranslate 0.5.0"

.SH NAME
.B LocalTranslate
- Translate offline using Firefox Translation Models

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B localtranslate
.RI [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RI [ \-\-help\-all ]
.RI [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.RI [ \-\-list\-languages ]
.br
.RS
.RI [ \-\-from=<from> ] " " [ \-\-to=<to> ] " "
.RI <text>

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B LocalTranslate
: Translate offline using Firefox Translation Models.
.br
LocalTranslate uses Firefox’s neural translation models (from mozilla/firefox-translations-models[1]) to perform high-quality translations locally on your device.
.br
.br
.PP
Read from stdin via a pipe when no text is given in args:
.RS
.nf
echo "Good Morning" | localtranslate --from=en --to=de
.fi
.RE

.I Kindly note that LocalTranslate is not affiliated with The Mozilla Foundation in any way.
.br
.I LocalTranslate is just a wrapper which lets you natively use Firefox’s neural translation models.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Displays help on commandline options

.TP
.B \-\-help-all
Displays help, including generic Qt options

.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Displays version information

.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
List available languages

.TP
.B \-\-from=<from>
Source language code (ISO code, e.g., ja, te, ml)

.TP
.B \-\-to=<to>
Target langugae code (ISO code, e.g., en, de, fr)

.SH AUTHORS
LocalTranslate is primarily written/maintained by Shriram Ravindranathan and Akash Doppalapudi. Contributions have come from various people on the GitHub repository[2], you can see contributors there.

